## Goal

Phantom rematch offers end: `RematchBook` records each entry's `finished_at`, and a read past `finished_at + REMATCH_OFFER_TTL_MS` drops an unmet entry, so `seen()` returns `opponent_offer: None` and no Accept button can lead to a `Lapsed` rejection. Entries that already made a game stay findable by late pollers (R3694000). The shared rematch suite, the server rematch suite, and `cargo jackioh spec check` all pass.

## Files to touch

| File | New/change | What changes |
|---|---|---|
| `crates/shared/src/host/rematch.rs` | change | `RematchEntry.finished_at: Option<i64>` field; `live_entry` stale condition; `offer` records/refreshes it; doc comments |
| `crates/shared/tests/rematch.rs` | change | Replace phantom-read test with `r2685000_a_read_past_the_window_drops_an_unmet_offer`; rework TTL-edge test as `r2685000_an_offer_at_the_windows_end_is_still_read_and_dropped_after` |
| `docs/implicit-states.md` | change | §14 Fields line (add `finished_at`); O10 row (now specified, new test); O12 row (new combination and test) |
| `apps/web/src/wire/generated/RematchEntry.ts` | change | Regenerated by the `ts` feature run; never hand-edited |

Do not touch: `sweep()`, `crates/shared/src/host/again.rs`, anything under `crates/server/`, `spec/`, `apps/` (outside the one generated file), or `.github/`, `.harness/`, `.squishy/`, `bot/`. Governing and already-correct: R2685000 (mandates the drop), R3694000 (pins preserved claims and the sweep), SPEC §9.5 rematch paragraph.

## Steps

1. In `crates/shared/src/host/rematch.rs`, add to `RematchEntry` after the `at` field (before `match_id`), copying the `Option<i64>` ts pattern from `crates/shared/src/host/boundary.rs:121`:
```rust
/// The finished match's end, as the offer that made this entry named it. R2685000 counts
/// the offer window from it, so a read past it drops an unmet entry even while its latest
/// offer is still under the TTL.
#[cfg_attr(feature = "ts", ts(type = "number | null"))]
pub finished_at: Option<i64>,
```
2. In the same file, widen `live_entry`'s stale condition so an unmet entry is stale past the window too:
```rust
entry.match_id.is_none()
    && (now - entry.at > REMATCH_OFFER_TTL_MS
        || !in_rematch_window(entry.finished_at, now))
```
Update its doc comment (lines 189-192) to say a read past the finished match's window drops an unmet entry (R2685000), and leave the claimed-entry arm exactly as is.
3. In the same file's `offer()`, add `finished_at,` to the `RematchEntry` literal (shorthand for the existing parameter), and after `entry.at = now;` add `entry.finished_at = finished_at;`. Do not change `sweep()`, `release()`, `seen()`'s signature, or any server caller.
4. In `crates/shared/tests/rematch.rs`, replace the test at lines 285-304 (doc comment included) with:
```rust
/// R2685000: a read past the finished match's window drops an unmet entry, so no offer nothing
/// can meet is ever shown (#4686, docs/implicit-states.md §14 O10).
#[test]
fn r2685000_a_read_past_the_window_drops_an_unmet_offer() {
    let mut book = book_with(&[(P1, STAKE_NORMAL)], END + 5);
    let past = END + REMATCH_OFFER_TTL_MS + 1;
    let seen = book.seen("m1", P2, past);
    assert_eq!(
        (seen.you_offered, seen.opponent_offer, seen.match_id),
        (None, None, None)
    );
    assert!(book.is_empty());
}
```
5. In the same test file, replace the TTL-edge test at lines 210-222 (doc comment included) with the window-based version, since an offer exactly TTL-old by `at` is now past the window and dropped:
```rust
/// R2685000: the window runs from the finished match's end to the TTL inclusive: an offer is
/// still read at the window's last moment, and a read past it drops the unmet entry.
#[test]
fn r2685000_an_offer_at_the_windows_end_is_still_read_and_dropped_after() {
    let mut book = book_with(&[(P1, STAKE_NORMAL)], END);
    book.offer("m2", Some(END), P1, STAKE_NORMAL, None, END, "g1");
    assert_eq!((book.len(), book.is_empty()), (2, false));
    let edge = END + REMATCH_OFFER_TTL_MS;
    assert!(book.seen("m1", P1, edge).you_offered.is_some());
    assert_eq!(book.len(), 2);
    assert!(book.seen("m1", P1, edge + 1).you_offered.is_none());
    assert_eq!(book.len(), 1);
}
```
6. In `docs/implicit-states.md` §14: in Fields (line 733), insert `` `finished_at` `` (the finished match's end, from the offer that made the entry) beside `` `at` ``. Rewrite O10's Expected to "Past the window an unmet entry is dropped as it is read, so no offer nothing can meet is shown (R2685000)" with Does pointing at the new step-4 test. Rewrite O12's combination to "an offer at the window's last moment", Expected to "Still read at `finished_at + REMATCH_OFFER_TTL_MS`, dropped a millisecond later; the window is the TTL inclusive (R2685000)", Does to the step-5 test. Leave §"For a person" audit history alone.
7. Regenerate the wire type by running the shared rematch tests with the `ts` feature (Tests), then `git status --porcelain`: the only generated diff must be `RematchEntry.ts` gaining `finishedAt: number | null`.

## Tests

- `cargo test -p jackioh-shared --features jackioh-engine/testkit --test shared rematch` — the rewritten tests plus the untouched R3694000, sweep, and JSON round-trip tests. Note: the issue's `--test rematch` names no target (`autotests = false`, one binary `shared`); this is the correct command.
- Same command with `--features ts,jackioh-engine/testkit` — writes the generated `RematchEntry.ts`; commit its diff.
- `cargo test -p jackioh-server --test server rematch` — unchanged server suite stays green (its reads run on frozen `now_ms`, inside the window).
- `cargo fmt --check`; `cargo clippy -p jackioh-shared --all-targets --features jackioh-engine/testkit -- -D warnings`; `cargo jackioh spec check` (R2685000's `proven_in` still resolves: the file keeps `r2685000` tests).

## Done when

- [ ] `RematchEntry` carries `finished_at`, set on create and refreshed on each taken offer.
- [ ] `seen()` past the window returns all-`None` and empties an unmet entry; claimed entries survive reads (R3694000 test green).
- [ ] TTL-edge behavior follows the window (step-5 test), not offer age.
- [ ] O10/O12/Fields docs match the code and name the new tests.
- [ ] Generated `RematchEntry.ts` diff committed; `spec check`, fmt, clippy, shared and server rematch tests pass.

## Risks

- `sweep()` deliberately untouched: R3694000's Rejected pins it keeping entries TTL-after-latest-offer; only reads gain the window check.
- No new ruling and no `spec/pending/4686.md`: R2685000's note already orders unmade-game entries dropped, so the fix implements existing words (a new R4686xxx was rejected as it would specify nothing new).
- No server changes needed: `seen()`/`offer()` signatures are unchanged, and server tests cannot observe the new path (paused-clock `now_ms` never leaves the window).
- `RematchBook` is memory-only (a restart drops it, O1), so the new field needs no `serde(default)` version shim.

## Open questions

None.

